  "name": "Solar-Feather Raiment",
  "type": "equipment",
  "img": "icons/equipment/chest/robe-layered-white.webp",
  "folder": "ggcgCjDNEDBTvbfE",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>White cloth sewn with feathers that are warm to the touch. In a dark room the raiment gives off the gray light of the hour before sunrise, and roosters crow when it is carried past.</p><p>While you wear this raiment and no armor, your Armor Class is 15 plus your Dexterity modifier. You have a Fly Speed of 60 feet and Resistance to Radiant damage.</p><p><strong>Daybreak.</strong> Once per day, as an action, you spread the raiment and it blazes. Each creature of your choice within 30 feet makes a [[/save ability=con dc=20 format=long]], taking [[/damage 10d6 type=radiant]] damage and having the Blinded condition for 1 minute on a failed save, or taking half as much damage only on a success. The raiment regains this power at dawn.</p><p><strong>No Shadow Falls.</strong> The wearer casts no shadow, and no darkness, mundane or magical, quite closes over them: they are always seen as a figure in faint dawn light. Those who look at the wearer cannot make themselves believe a lie the wearer tells for gain.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
